---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="ShadowADJ — speech practice & reflection">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-cyan/80">Real-time speech reflection</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
      A mirror for how you speak —<br />not a judge of who you are.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-white/60">
      ShadowADJ listens to a live answer and shows the things a good coach notices: pace, pauses,
      filler words, vocabulary variety, how long you take before you start. Built for debate
      practice, interview prep, and speech coaching.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex gap-3">
      <a href="/console" class="btn btn-primary">Open the console →</a>
      <a href="/about" class="btn">Why it works this way</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="glass p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Descriptive, not accusatory</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/55">
          No risk score. No “review” verdict. No guess about whether an answer was AI-assisted —
          that can’t be done reliably from speech and ShadowADJ doesn’t try.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Consent-first</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/55">
          A session can’t start until the person being recorded says yes. They see the exact same
          dashboard as everyone else in the room.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="glass p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">Nothing kept</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/55">
          Audio stays in memory and is discarded when the session ends. Summaries live in your
          browser’s local storage — there’s no account and no server-side profile.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
